{"id": "EUVD-2026-71239", "enisaUuid": "55d3f0a6-9a52-31e0-ab09-b21825c48600", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: restore nofs context unconditionally in xfs_trans_roll\n\nWhen __xfs_trans_commit() fails in xfs_trans_roll(), the NOFS context\nis cleared but only restored in the success path.  This leaves the\nerror path without nofs protection, causing a circular lock dependency\nbetween xfs_nondir_ilock_class and fs_reclaim:\n\n       CPU0                    CPU1\n       ----                    ----\n  lock(&xfs_nondir_ilock_class);\n                               lock(fs_reclaim);\n                               lock(&xfs_nondir_ilock_class);\n  lock(fs_reclaim);\n\nFix this by moving xfs_trans_set_context() before the error check so\nthat nofs context is always restored on the new transaction.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:13:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:43:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b09198cf90ccf296970b774beea1c1ddb260f94c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d00a39c676274f4071b467e630565ac1e3ae0f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0241ea5fb0fe86d2a673163b2f5815111aadc7f7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m2xq-p36j-8h55", "CVE-2026-80804"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2c2bda4b-51d2-3a62-ae5a-6c3a1bebb8cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3d73e1c4-c7a1-3b89-9c15-7054fc18d5ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a1ca658d649a4d8972e2e21ac2625b633217e327 <b09198cf90ccf296970b774beea1c1ddb260f94c"}, {"id": "79ea9f84-5105-3f75-867d-8f7a43d446c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a1ca658d649a4d8972e2e21ac2625b633217e327 <0241ea5fb0fe86d2a673163b2f5815111aadc7f7"}, {"id": "9a3d4c63-c3fc-35df-817d-d7a568ef93a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a0424f92-6d50-3bad-9192-88d8c1a81e88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "b6b00fe8-3578-38a1-99e6-103929bceb74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.11"}, {"id": "cbbb3e8d-ccbe-3279-a9fc-1af2dcb67595", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.1"}, {"id": "d552653f-9074-3662-bc24-e9105c8b6536", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a1ca658d649a4d8972e2e21ac2625b633217e327 <4d00a39c676274f4071b467e630565ac1e3ae0f2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fa7427ba-24fa-33fa-ab26-fd912983ac41", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}